' ============================================================================
'  deathtext.cut -- YOU / DIED, falling in and landing hard.
'
'  Short on purpose (about 5 seconds): it is the reference for ANIMATED TEXT,
'  and a 90-second showcase is no use when you are iterating on the timing of
'  one landing.
'
'  Three things have to line up or the hit does not read:
'    * `from 66,-8` starts the caption ABOVE the screen, so it falls in rather
'      than appearing.
'    * `ease bounce` gives it the landing. `out` would settle politely; bounce
'      is what makes it feel like weight.
'    * the thud and the shake are SEPARATE lines after a `wait`, timed to the
'      moment it lands -- firing them with the caption would sound the impact
'      while the text was still in the air.
' ============================================================================

scene deathtext
dev                      ' a showcase, not a story beat: kept out of the Storybook
storybook "You Died" "Animated text: falling, landing, and the shake."

var display$ = "alagard.ttf"
var blood    = #cc1111

show bg "bg/cut-crypt.png" fill
cam 0.5,0.5 zoom 1.4
fade to black over 0
fade from black over 0.5

musicstop fade 0.3

' --------------------------------------------------------------- "YOU"
caption "YOU" at 66,13 from 66,-8 over 0.9 ease bounce anchor c color blood font display$ 96
wait 0.85
sfx "chamber-enter"
shake 9 for 0.6

' --------------------------------------------------------------- "DIED"
caption "DIED" at 66,26 from 66,-12 over 1.0 ease bounce anchor c color blood font display$ 96
wait 0.95
sfx "boom"
shake 14 for 0.9
flash blood 0.22

' the epitaph arrives quietly, from the side, once the shouting is over
caption "{name} the {class}, {level} levels down" at 66,38 from 20,38 over 1.2 ease outcubic anchor c color #7a6a6a font display$ 22
wait 2.2

crtoff 0.9
